}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC1A",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type AC1A model. The model represents the fieldcontrolled alternatorrectifier excitation systems designated type AC1A. These excitation systems consist of an alternator main exciter with noncontrolled rectifiers.Reference IEEE 421.52005 6.1."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEAC1A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC2A",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type AC2A model. The model represents a high initial response fieldcontrolled alternatorrectifier excitation system. The alternator main exciter is used with noncontrolled rectifiers. The type AC2A model is similar to that of type AC1A except for the inclusion of exciter time constant compensation and exciter field current limiting elements.Reference IEEE 421.52005 6.2."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEAC2A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC2A.kb",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Second stage regulator gain iKiisubBsubi gt 0.  Typical value  25."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC2A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "kb"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PU"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC3A",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type AC3A model. The model represents the fieldcontrolled alternatorrectifier excitation systems designated type AC3A. These excitation systems include an alternator main exciter with noncontrolled rectifiers. The exciter employs selfexcitation and the voltage regulator power is derived from the exciter output voltage.  Therefore this system has an additional nonlinearity simulated by the use of a multiplier whose inputs are the voltage regulator command signal iVai and the exciter output voltage iEfdi times iKiisubRsubi.  This model is applicable to excitation systems employing static voltage regulators.Reference IEEE 421.52005 6.3."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEAC3A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC4A",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type AC4A model. The model represents type AC4A alternatorsupplied controlledrectifier excitation system which is quite different from the other types of AC systems. This high initial response excitation system utilizes a full thyristor bridge in the exciter output circuit.  The voltage regulator controls the firing of the thyristor bridges. The exciter alternator uses an independent voltage regulator to control its output voltage to a constant value. These effects are not modelled however transient loading effects on the exciter alternator are included.Reference IEEE 421.52005 6.4."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEAC4A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC5A",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type AC5A model. The model represents a simplified model for brushless excitation systems. The regulator is supplied from a source such as a permanent magnet generator which is not affected by system disturbances.  Unlike other AC models this model uses loaded rather than open circuit exciter saturation data in the same way as it is used for the DC models.  Because the model has been widely implemented by the industry it is sometimes used to represent other types of systems when either detailed data for them are not available or simplified models are required.Reference IEEE 421.52005 6.5."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEAC5A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC6A",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type AC6A model. The model represents fieldcontrolled alternatorrectifier excitation systems with systemsupplied electronic voltage regulators.  The maximum output of the regulator iViisubRsubi is a function of terminal voltage iViisubTsubi. The field current limiter included in the original model AC6A remains in the 2005 update.Reference IEEE 421.52005 6.6. "
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEAC6A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC7B",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type AC7B model. The model represents excitation systems which consist of an AC alternator with either stationary or rotating rectifiers to produce the DC field requirements. It is an upgrade to earlier AC excitation systems which replace only the controls but retain the AC alternator and diode rectifier bridge.Reference IEEE 421.52005 6.7. Note however that in IEEE 421.52005 the 1  isTiisubEsubi block is shown as 1  1  isTiisubEsubi which is incorrect."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEAC7B"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC7B.kf1",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Excitation control system stabilizer gain iKiisubF1subi gt 0.  Typical value  0212."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC7B"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "kf1"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PU"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC7B.kf2",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Excitation control system stabilizer gain iKiisubF2subi gt 0.  Typical value  0."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC7B"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "kf2"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PU"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC7B.kf3",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Excitation control system stabilizer gain iKiisubF3subi gt 0.  Typical value  0."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC7B"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "kf3"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PU"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC7B.kl",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Exciter field voltage lower limit parameter iKiisubLsubi.  Typical value  10."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC7B"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "kl"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PU"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC7B.kpa",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Voltage regulator proportional gain iKiisubPAsubi gt 0 if ExcIEEEAC7B.kia  0.  Typical value  6536."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC7B"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "kpa"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PU"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEAC8B",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type AC8B model. This model represents a PID voltage regulator with either a brushless exciter or DC exciter. The AVR in this model consists of PID control with separate constants for the proportional iKiisubPRsubi integral iKiisubIRsubi and derivative iKiisubDRsubi gains. The representation of the brushless exciter iTiisubEsubi iKiisubEsubi iSiisubEsubi iKiisubCsubi iKiisubDsubi is similar to the model type AC2A. The type AC8B model can be used to represent static voltage regulators applied to brushless excitation systems. Digitally based voltage regulators feeding DC rotating main exciters can be represented with the AC type AC8B model with the parameters iKiisubCsubi and iKiisubDsubi set to 0.  For thyristor power stages fed from the generator terminals the limits iViisubRMAXsubi and iViisubRMINsubii ishould be a function of terminal voltage VisubTsubi x iViisubRMAXsubisub suband iViisubTsubi x iViisubRMINsubi.Reference IEEE 421.52005 6.8. "
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEAC8B"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEDC1A",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type DC1A model. This model represents fieldcontrolled DC commutator exciters with continuously acting voltage regulators especially the directacting rheostatic rotating amplifier and magnetic amplifier types.  Because this model has been widely implemented by the industry it is sometimes used to represent other types of systems when detailed data for them are not available or when a simplified model is required.Reference IEEE 421.52005 5.1. "
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEDC1A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEDC2A",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type DC2A model. This model represents fieldcontrolled DC commutator exciters with continuously acting voltage regulators having supplies obtained from the generator or auxiliary bus.  It differs from the type DC1A model only in the voltage regulator output limits which are now proportional to terminal voltage iViisubTsubi.It is representative of solidstate replacements for various forms of older mechanical and rotating amplifier regulating equipment connected to DC commutator exciters.Reference IEEE 421.52005 5.2. "
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEDC2A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEDC2A.exclim",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "iexclimi.  IEEE standard is ambiguous about lower limit on exciter output. Typical value   999  which means that there is no limit applied."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEDC2A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "exclim"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PU"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEDC3A",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type DC3A model. This model represents older systems in particular those DC commutator exciters with noncontinuously acting regulators that were commonly used before the development of the continuously acting varieties.  These systems respond at basically two different rates depending upon the magnitude of voltage error. For small errors adjustment is made periodically with a signal to a motoroperated rheostat. Larger errors cause resistors to be quickly shorted or inserted and a strong forcing signal applied to the exciter. Continuous motion of the motoroperated rheostat occurs for these larger error signals even though it is bypassed by contactor action.Reference IEEE 421.52005 5.3. "
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEDC3A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEDC4B",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type DC4B model. These excitation systems utilize a fieldcontrolled DC commutator exciter with a continuously acting voltage regulator having supplies obtained from the generator or auxiliary bus.Reference IEEE 421.52005 5.4. "
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEDC4B"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEDC4B.kd",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Regulator derivative gain iKiisubDsubi gt 0.  Typical value  20."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEDC4B"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "kd"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PU"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEDC4B.ki",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
