}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEST2A",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type ST2A model. Some static systems use both current and voltage sources generator terminal quantities to comprise the power source.  The regulator controls the exciter output through controlled saturation of the power transformer components.  These compoundsource rectifier excitation systems are designated type ST2A and are represented by ExcIEEEST2A.Reference IEEE 421.52005 7.2. "
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEST2A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEST3A",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type ST3A model.  Some static systems utilize a field voltage control loop to linearize the exciter control characteristic. This also makes the output independent of supply source variations until supply limitations are reached.  These systems utilize a variety of controlledrectifier designs full thyristor complements or hybrid bridges in either series or shunt configurations. The power source can consist of only a potential source either fed from the machine terminals or from internal windings. Some designs can have compound power sources utilizing both machine potential and current. These power sources are represented as phasor combinations of machine terminal current and voltage and are accommodated by suitable parameters in model type ST3A which is represented by ExcIEEEST3A.Reference IEEE 421.52005 7.3. "
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEST3A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEST3A.ka",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Voltage regulator gain iKiisubAsubi gt 0. This is parameter iKi in the IEEE standard. Typical value  200."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEST3A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ka"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PU"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEST3A.vmmax",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Maximum inner loop output iViisubMMaxsubi gt 0.  Typical value  1."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEST3A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "vmmax"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PU"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEST3A.vmmin",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Minimum inner loop output iViisubMMinsubi lt 0.  Typical value  0."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEST3A"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "vmmin"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PU"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEST4B",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type ST4B model. This model is a variation of the type ST3A model with a proportional plus integral PI regulator block replacing the laglead regulator characteristic that is in the ST3A model. Both potential and compound source rectifier excitation systems are modelled.  The PI regulator blocks have nonwindup limits that are represented. The voltage regulator of this model is typically implemented digitally.Reference IEEE 421.52005 7.4. "
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEST4B"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEST5B",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "IEEE 421.52005 type ST5B model. The type ST5B excitation system is a variation of the type ST1A model with alternative overexcitation and underexcitation inputs and additional limits.The block diagram in the IEEE 421.5 standard has input signal iVc iand does not indicate the summation point with iVrefi. The implementation of the ExcIEEEST5B shall consider summation point with iVrefi.Reference IEEE 421.52005 7.5. "
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ExcIEEEST5B"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcitationSystemDynamics"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEST5B.kr",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Regulator gain iKiisubRsubi gt 0.  Typical value  200."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ExcIEEEST5B"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
