  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Fluid power factor at specified temperature in percent. Commonly used in US. Note Fluid power factor is very similar to fluid dissapation factor but fluid power factor is cosine of the phase angle between an AC voltage applied to oil and the resulting current where dissipation factor is the tangent. For values up to 0.005 fluid power factor and dissapation factor are very close. There is a conversion equation between the two. "
  } ],
